{%- comment -%}
  AI Visibility - the comparison table's markup, once (PRD §4.8,
  PRD-AI-READABILITY P0.2).

  Rendered by the comparison-table app block and by the visible content
  snippet on collection pages, so the two cannot drift apart. Arguments:

    table           the collection's $app.table value: columns, rows
    caption         the caption text, read by screen readers
    shop_url        shop.url, for the product links
    product_column  label of the first column; when blank, "Product" in the
                    storefront's language (locales/*.json, content.product_column)
    header_border   CSS border under the header row
    row_border      CSS border under each row, 'none' for none

  The comparison-table block passes the borders it has always had. The
  content block passes a plain rule under the header and none between rows,
  so it sets no colour of its own.

  Renders nothing unless there is at least one column and one row: an
  empty table is worse than no table. Every value escaped.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if table and table.columns.size > 0 and table.rows.size > 0 -%}
  {%- assign av_t_head = header_border | default: '1px solid' -%}
  {%- assign av_t_row = row_border | default: 'none' -%}
  {%- assign av_t_first = product_column -%}
  {%- if av_t_first == blank -%}{%- assign av_t_first = 'content.product_column' | t -%}{%- endif -%}
  <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
    <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse;">
      <caption class="visually-hidden">{{ caption | escape }}</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col" style="text-align: left; padding: 0.5rem; border-bottom: {{ av_t_head }};">
            {{ av_t_first | escape }}
          </th>
          {%- for column in table.columns -%}
            <th scope="col" style="text-align: left; padding: 0.5rem; border-bottom: {{ av_t_head }};">
              {{ column | escape }}
            </th>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {%- for row in table.rows -%}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" style="text-align: left; font-weight: 400; padding: 0.5rem; border-bottom: {{ av_t_row }};">
              {%- if row.handle != blank -%}
                <a href="{{ shop_url }}/products/{{ row.handle }}">{{ row.title | escape }}</a>
              {%- else -%}
                {{ row.title | escape }}
              {%- endif -%}
            </th>
            {%- for cell in row.cells -%}
              <td style="padding: 0.5rem; border-bottom: {{ av_t_row }};">
                {%- comment -%}
                  A blank cell is honest: the description did not say. Filling
                  it with a dash or a guess would be worse than the gap.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {{ cell | escape }}
              </td>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </tr>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
